gine/godot/issues/comments/2705010286","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103661#issuecomment-2705010286","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103661","id":2705010286,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hOy5u","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T21:44:10Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T21:44:10Z","body":"> It does _not_ work fully with an individual Joy-Con (L) or Joy-Con (R). When held horizontally, the left, up, and right buttons do not register in Godot; the down button registers as \"Nintendo Y\" (Joypad Button 2).\r\n\r\nThis happens for me as well, both before and after these changes. It seems to be a result of moving to the Game Controller framework so I'm not sure if there's a way to work around it. In any case it should be orthogonal to this PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2705010286/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"min